273
00:23:35,920 --> 00:23:39,160
You're the one who kept showing off,
paying loads of money. I'm genuinely shocked.

274
00:23:43,520 --> 00:23:45,400
Stop making excuses.

275
00:23:45,400 --> 00:23:48,080
You love her, so you pay for her. That's it.

276
00:23:49,120 --> 00:23:52,040
And why did you bring David along
to show off to her?

277
00:23:52,680 --> 00:23:54,600
Because she was there with Techin.

278
00:23:54,600 --> 00:23:57,800
Peem, it's just me here. Stop being so stubborn.

279
00:24:02,920 --> 00:24:04,840
Fine, I was irritated.

280
00:24:06,360 --> 00:24:09,000
Irritated? You're jealous!

281
00:24:09,000 --> 00:24:10,720
It's called being jealous.

282
00:24:10,720 --> 00:24:11,560
I wasn't.

283
00:24:11,560 --> 00:24:12,960
Don't deny it.

284
00:24:12,960 --> 00:24:15,480
You were being all touchy with David,

285
00:24:15,480 --> 00:24:17,160
not because you felt irritated,

286
00:24:17,160 --> 00:24:19,080
but because you're jealous.

287
00:24:19,080 --> 00:24:20,760
Jealous. Jealous.

288
00:24:21,360 --> 00:24:23,120
There's no way it's because you're irritated.

289
00:24:25,280 --> 00:24:29,080
It's like, "You have a new guy?
I can have a new guy too."

290
00:24:29,400 --> 00:24:30,320
Right?

291
00:24:33,080 --> 00:24:33,800
Yeah.

292
00:24:36,680 --> 00:24:37,640
You poor thing.

293
00:24:38,360 --> 00:24:40,200
If you love her and miss her so much

294
00:24:40,200 --> 00:24:42,560
that you'll act confused
and go to her place when you're drunk

295
00:24:42,560 --> 00:24:44,400
even though she already has a new boyfriend,

296
00:24:45,160 --> 00:24:48,360
you need to start thinking about
how you're going to deal with yourself.

297
00:24:57,040 --> 00:24:58,600
I need to stop loving her, right?

298
00:24:59,600 --> 00:25:00,440
Yeah.

299
00:25:18,880 --> 00:25:20,280
Hello, Dad.

300
00:25:21,360 --> 00:25:22,640
Oh, Peem.

301
00:25:25,080 --> 00:25:26,280
Can I talk to you for a sec?

302
00:25:34,880 --> 00:25:37,560
You're late for work.
Some days, you didn't show up at all.

303
00:25:37,560 --> 00:25:39,160
You get drunk all the time.

304
00:25:39,640 --> 00:25:42,360
Apart from David's matter,
you barely touch anything else.

305
00:25:43,200 --> 00:25:45,440
You even kept a client waiting in a meeting.

306
00:25:45,920 --> 00:25:48,080
The documents weren't signed.
The checks won't go through.

307
00:25:49,560 --> 00:25:50,880
What is going on, Peem?

308
00:25:52,720 --> 00:25:53,920
I'm sorry, Dad.

309
00:25:54,960 --> 00:25:57,360
Work has been piling up on your end
for a week now.

310
00:25:57,360 --> 00:26:00,200
Do you need to get in the mood
before you can sign it?

311
00:26:01,120 --> 00:26:03,600
You can't work like this.
The company needs to keep going.

312
00:26:03,600 --> 00:26:05,040
Now, everything has ground to a halt.

313
00:26:05,720 --> 00:26:07,400
How are the others supposed to
get their work done?

314
00:26:09,920 --> 00:26:11,520
I'll be better.

315
00:26:13,120 --> 00:26:15,480
Just go back to being your old self, Peem.

316
00:26:17,200 --> 00:26:20,400
Seriously, what's going on?

317
00:26:24,360 --> 00:26:26,840
I will go back to being my old self, Dad.

318
00:26:29,160 --> 00:26:31,240
I want to know, as your father.

319
00:26:34,440 --> 00:26:35,680
What happened?

320
00:26:45,320 --> 00:26:48,520
Does this woman really affect you this much?

321
00:26:54,040 --> 00:26:56,200
Peem, it's okay to be sad.

322
00:26:57,360 --> 00:27:01,360
But you can't let your personal issues
ruin everything like this.

323
00:27:18,960 --> 00:27:20,320
Whoa!

324
00:27:20,320 --> 00:27:21,520
Can I eat them now?

325
00:27:21,520 --> 00:27:23,200
They all look so tasty.

326
00:27:23,200 --> 00:27:24,240
Try them for me.

327
00:27:24,560 --> 00:27:26,160
And tell me if they're good or not.

328
00:27:26,160 --> 00:27:27,000
Sure.

329
00:27:29,840 --> 00:27:31,040
Whoa!

330
00:27:34,120 --> 00:27:35,280
Mmm.

331
00:27:35,800 --> 00:27:37,600
It's so soft and not too sweet.

332
00:27:37,600 --> 00:27:38,720
What do you think, Miew?

333
00:27:42,200 --> 00:27:43,080
Miew.

334
00:27:44,360 --> 00:27:45,360
Miew!

335
00:27:46,680 --> 00:27:48,200
Parn asked you. Didn't you hear?

336
00:27:48,200 --> 00:27:51,080
Oh, right, it's very soft. It melted in my mouth.

337
00:27:52,640 --> 00:27:53,640
Mmm.

338
00:27:57,560 --> 00:27:59,480
What about you? How are you?

339
00:28:05,440 --> 00:28:08,040
Okay, you don't have to say anything.

340
00:28:08,360 --> 00:28:09,680
I can tell it from your face.

341
00:28:32,800 --> 00:28:33,920
Your shop looks nice.

342
00:28:36,800 --> 00:28:37,800
Thank you.

343
00:28:39,160 --> 00:28:41,480
But you didn't come here
to admire my shop, did you?

344
00:28:42,640 --> 00:28:46,440
You know that Peem will have to take over
the company from me, right?

345
00:28:47,760 --> 00:28:48,680
Yes.

346
00:28:49,760 --> 00:28:53,200
Honestly, I don't have a problem
if she likes women.

347
00:28:54,360 --> 00:28:55,880
But I have a problem

348
00:28:56,680 --> 00:28:58,120
with her loving someone like you.

349
00:29:00,360 --> 00:29:01,400
Like me?

350
00:29:01,960 --> 00:29:02,960
Yes.

351
00:29:03,520 --> 00:29:04,880
A sex worker like you.

352
00:29:07,560 --> 00:29:10,080
Even though you don't do that anymore,

353
00:29:10,080 --> 00:29:13,000
those who knew you, or have met you,

354
00:29:13,000 --> 00:29:15,720
will still remember what you've done.

355
00:29:18,960 --> 00:29:20,640
Even if Peem doesn't care,

356
00:29:21,840 --> 00:29:24,080
people in her social circle

357
00:29:25,960 --> 00:29:27,640
won't stop talking about it.

358
00:29:31,800 --> 00:29:35,800
The fact that Peem's mother
is a sex worker is bad enough as it is.

359
00:29:37,200 --> 00:29:39,600
I don't want her to follow in my footsteps.

360
00:29:42,800 --> 00:29:44,080
If you love Peem,

361
00:29:45,480 --> 00:29:46,520
let her go.

362
00:29:56,400 --> 00:30:00,080
And if you need money, contact my secretary.

363
00:30:06,440 --> 00:30:07,280
Come on.

364
00:30:09,000 --> 00:30:11,040
Parn, what did he say to you?

365
00:30:21,960 --> 00:30:23,720
(Mom)

366
00:30:29,280 --> 00:30:31,520
Parn, your mom is calling.

367
00:30:32,200 --> 00:30:34,120
Hey, you should just ignore it for now.

368
00:30:38,520 --> 00:30:40,400
If I ignore it, she'll keep calling.

369
00:30:41,440 --> 00:30:42,520
In the end, I'll have to answer.

370
00:30:47,000 --> 00:30:48,040
Parn.

371
00:30:48,040 --> 00:30:49,600
Send me some money.

372
00:30:50,920 --> 00:30:52,360
I'm in real trouble.

373
00:30:54,160 --> 00:30:55,760
I don't have it, Mom.

374
00:30:55,760 --> 00:30:57,360
I don't have any more for you.

375
00:31:07,120 --> 00:31:08,040
What did she say?

376
00:31:08,520 --> 00:31:09,800
She said she didn't have anymore.

377
00:31:13,960 --> 00:31:15,040
How's that possible?

378
00:31:16,160 --> 00:31:19,000
I'm not stupid enough to believe
she doesn't have any money.

379
00:31:22,120 --> 00:31:24,160
It’s no surprise that she doesn’t have any.

380
00:31:25,360 --> 00:31:26,880
She spent millions paying her father's debts.

381
00:31:27,720 --> 00:31:28,920
She doesn't have it.

382
00:31:29,520 --> 00:31:31,240
And do you have it to give to me, huh?

383
00:31:33,160 --> 00:31:35,760
A lowly salary man like you
doesn't have the money to give to me.

384
00:31:36,880 --> 00:31:38,880
If you don't have it, I don't need your opinion.

385
00:31:43,840 --> 00:31:45,480
You have Parn's girlfriend's phone number, right?

386
00:31:47,080 --> 00:31:49,960
Parn doesn't have it, but she does.

387
00:31:50,840 --> 00:31:51,680
Call her.

388
00:31:52,360 --> 00:31:53,440
Leave her alone, Dad.

389
00:31:56,240 --> 00:31:57,480
I said call her.

390
00:32:00,400 --> 00:32:01,160
Mom.

391
00:32:04,240 --> 00:32:05,280
I said call her!

392
00:32:14,080 --> 00:32:15,520
Miew, are you putting in any effort?

393
00:32:15,880 --> 00:32:16,960
It hit my foot.

394
00:32:16,960 --> 00:32:18,520
See? You're not lifting it.

395
00:32:18,520 --> 00:32:20,760
I am lifting it. Why are you so whiny?

396
00:32:20,760 --> 00:32:22,680
You ate a lot too.

397
00:32:22,680 --> 00:32:24,400
Just get the chair.

398
00:32:30,320 --> 00:32:32,600
You did the right thing,
not giving your mom the money.

399
00:32:32,600 --> 00:32:35,120
Stop it. Don't bring it up.

400
00:32:37,400 --> 00:32:39,720
Alright, let's go home. I'll give you a ride.

401
00:32:40,360 --> 00:32:43,480
Hey, how about we stop and pick up some food?

402
00:32:43,480 --> 00:32:44,680
Let's eat at your place.

403
00:32:55,160 --> 00:32:56,320
What is it, Pong?

404
00:33:02,640 --> 00:33:04,840
Here. The money you want.

405
00:33:14,440 --> 00:33:15,720
Thank you so much.

406
00:33:15,720 --> 00:33:18,160
I'll have Parn find the money to pay you back
as soon as possible.

407
00:33:19,440 --> 00:33:20,560
Dad.

408
00:33:21,320 --> 00:33:22,320
What's going on?

409
00:33:25,480 --> 00:33:27,480
Where are you taking my money?

410
00:33:27,480 --> 00:33:28,800
It's not your money.

411
00:33:30,560 --> 00:33:32,240
Why are you giving my dad money?

412
00:33:32,240 --> 00:33:34,600
Your family is in trouble.
I'm just trying to help.

413
00:33:34,600 --> 00:33:37,160
I didn't ask you to.
And it's none of your business.

414
00:33:38,120 --> 00:33:39,440
Stop it. Give me back my money.

415
00:33:39,440 --> 00:33:40,320
No!

416
00:33:41,040 --> 00:33:44,520
If you don't give this to me,
where do you expect me to find the money?

417
00:33:44,520 --> 00:33:47,120
Wherever you can, but not from Ms. Peem.

418
00:33:48,000 --> 00:33:48,800
Parn!

419
00:33:48,800 --> 00:33:50,080
- Don't!
- Dad!

420
00:33:51,440 --> 00:33:53,960
I'll take all the money back
if you touch Parn again.

421
00:34:14,280 --> 00:34:16,360
From now on, stay away from my family.

422
00:34:19,679 --> 00:34:21,920
You're in this much trouble
and you still dare to refuse?

423
00:34:23,560 --> 00:34:25,000
I know that you have money.

424
00:34:25,480 --> 00:34:26,920
But I don't want your money.

425
00:34:27,679 --> 00:34:30,440
The money you used to pay off my dad's debt,
I'll pay you back.

426
00:34:30,960 --> 00:34:31,880
No need.

427
00:34:31,880 --> 00:34:34,600
I will. I don't want to be indebted to anyone.

428
00:34:36,840 --> 00:34:37,719
Especially you.

429
00:34:42,400 --> 00:34:43,719
Do you hate me that much?

430
00:34:45,760 --> 00:34:48,880
If you love Peem, let her go.

431
00:34:51,480 --> 00:34:52,520
That's right.

432
00:34:54,199 --> 00:34:55,440
I hate you so much.

433
00:34:59,400 --> 00:35:01,320
You hate me so much
you don't want anything to do with me?

434
00:35:10,000 --> 00:35:11,160
Then I'll wait and see

435
00:35:12,040 --> 00:35:13,600
how you're going to find the money to pay me back.

436
00:35:15,400 --> 00:35:17,240
It's five million, Parn, not five hundred.

437
00:35:20,840 --> 00:35:23,000
But you have an easy way to make money, don't you?

438
00:35:25,120 --> 00:35:25,960
You're right.

439
00:35:26,480 --> 00:35:29,880
Don't forget that I'm Paradise's top angel.

440
00:35:42,200 --> 00:35:44,480
Parn! Why the hell did you have to butt in?

441
00:35:44,480 --> 00:35:45,680
Why did you stop her?

442
00:35:45,680 --> 00:35:46,880
Where am I supposed to get the money from now?

443
00:35:46,880 --> 00:35:48,720
Hit me. Hit me now.

444
00:35:48,720 --> 00:35:49,960
I don't have any more for you.

445
00:35:50,360 --> 00:35:53,280
Even if you beat me to death,
I don't have any money to give you.

446
00:35:56,720 --> 00:35:58,600
You want those loan sharks to kill me, right?

447
00:35:59,920 --> 00:36:00,880
Huh?!

448
00:36:01,600 --> 00:36:03,640
You've been saying that to me all my life.

449
00:36:04,080 --> 00:36:08,040
I paid off your debts countless times
but you kept going back to borrow from them.

450
00:36:08,440 --> 00:36:09,480
You never stopped.

451
00:36:09,960 --> 00:36:11,720
This time, I really don't have any to give you.

452
00:36:12,720 --> 00:36:15,920
You said you don't have money
but you're opening a new shop.

453
00:36:16,240 --> 00:36:17,920
Just sell your shop and give me the money.

454
00:36:17,920 --> 00:36:18,920
No!

455
00:36:18,920 --> 00:36:20,000
Parn.

456
00:36:20,000 --> 00:36:21,200
No, Mom.

457
00:36:21,200 --> 00:36:22,280
I'm not selling it.

458
00:36:25,120 --> 00:36:27,080
I'll use this shop to make a living.

459
00:36:27,440 --> 00:36:30,240
All this time, I've done what I could to help.

460
00:36:31,280 --> 00:36:34,760
But if that makes you think
I have to be responsible for everything you do,

461
00:36:35,960 --> 00:36:37,480
I will stop now.

462
00:36:40,280 --> 00:36:43,160
From now on, I won't give you two any more money.

463
00:36:44,800 --> 00:36:46,480
I want to try living for myself.

464
00:36:59,600 --> 00:37:01,400
Parn! You ungrateful child!

465
00:37:02,040 --> 00:37:03,760
Your life will never prosper!

466
00:37:10,040 --> 00:37:11,200
Who do you think you are?

467
00:37:11,920 --> 00:37:15,200
Don't forget that I'm Paradise's top angel.

468
00:37:16,160 --> 00:37:17,000
Of course.

469
00:37:17,440 --> 00:37:20,720
Paradise Club's Angel can make money easily
just by selling her body.

470
00:37:20,720 --> 00:37:23,720
Go ahead. Sell your body until you die.

471
00:37:24,200 --> 00:37:25,880
Since you've made your choice, go all out.

472
00:37:36,280 --> 00:37:38,120
Should I go see it with my own eyes?

473
00:37:40,640 --> 00:37:42,040
So I can finally get over it?

474
00:37:47,240 --> 00:37:48,960
Oh, Ms. Peem.

475
00:37:53,680 --> 00:37:55,120
Will Parn be in the auction today?

476
00:37:55,920 --> 00:37:57,320
Do you want to see Parn?

477
00:37:58,600 --> 00:37:59,520
No.

478
00:38:02,600 --> 00:38:04,720
Parn is no longer working here.

479
00:38:05,600 --> 00:38:08,360
The last day she came here was the day you came.

480
00:38:08,920 --> 00:38:11,720
Sis Mol called Parn
and asked her to come and help.

481
00:38:12,640 --> 00:38:14,040
She called her herself?

482
00:38:19,480 --> 00:38:21,520
Let's talk somewhere else.

483
00:38:26,680 --> 00:38:30,440
Since Parn started seeing you,
she hasn't been working here anymore.

484
00:38:30,440 --> 00:38:32,440
She even asked me

485
00:38:32,440 --> 00:38:34,440
to help tell Sis Mol she's going to quit.

486
00:38:35,480 --> 00:38:36,800
But she's still accepting clients.

487
00:38:37,360 --> 00:38:39,280
She even went out with Techin.

488
00:38:39,280 --> 00:38:40,800
Oh my. Well.

489
00:38:41,440 --> 00:38:45,160
Mr. Techin has been Parn's client for so long.

490
00:38:45,160 --> 00:38:47,720
So long I think they've become friends.

491
00:38:47,720 --> 00:38:51,680
I can't say much because
I don't want to reveal clients' secrets,

492
00:38:52,200 --> 00:38:57,320
but I can assure you there is nothing
between Parn and Mr. Techin.

493
00:39:00,000 --> 00:39:03,720
But I don't get it.
Why did she come back to work here?

494
00:39:07,680 --> 00:39:09,680
Sis Mol owed ten million to a loan shark.

495
00:39:10,520 --> 00:39:14,320
Parn came to help make money to pay off the debt,

496
00:39:14,320 --> 00:39:15,840
so they wouldn't take over this place.

497
00:39:15,840 --> 00:39:19,880
But after the debt had been settled,
Parn told Sis Mol she's going to stop right away.

498
00:39:20,800 --> 00:39:23,880
The day you came here was Paradise's Birthday.

499
00:39:23,880 --> 00:39:25,960
Sis Mol asked Parn to come join the event.

500
00:39:26,280 --> 00:39:27,560
Parn.

501
00:39:28,880 --> 00:39:29,960
Ms. Peem is here.

502
00:39:31,040 --> 00:39:33,560
Parn, she's buying 500 drinks. What do you say?

503
00:39:33,560 --> 00:39:37,600
Hey, but you're not here to work.
You're just here for the event.

504
00:39:38,120 --> 00:39:39,920
Right, Sis only asked you to join.

505
00:39:40,280 --> 00:39:41,280
That's right.

506
00:39:43,680 --> 00:39:46,600
If I go in, she might listen to my explanation.

507
00:39:47,120 --> 00:39:49,440
Parn wasn't going to be in the auction.

508
00:39:50,160 --> 00:39:54,120
But since it's you,
she wanted to be your drink server.

509
00:39:56,640 --> 00:40:00,520
She's running a bakery now.
She's not coming back to work here.

510
00:40:02,200 --> 00:40:04,080
Do you know where her shop is?

511
00:40:05,720 --> 00:40:09,000
She asked me not to tell you no matter what.

512
00:40:36,680 --> 00:40:38,920
You got dumped too?

513
00:40:39,920 --> 00:40:41,160
Is that why you're drinking here?

514
00:40:43,840 --> 00:40:45,000
Who dumped me?

515
00:40:46,400 --> 00:40:47,400
Parn, of course.

516
00:40:48,160 --> 00:40:49,800
She's not accepting any more jobs.

517
00:40:53,400 --> 00:40:55,320
I'm bummed she stopped accepting jobs.

518
00:40:55,840 --> 00:40:57,200
But I'm not sad.

519
00:41:02,360 --> 00:41:03,600
Didn't she tell you

520
00:41:05,080 --> 00:41:06,280
that I'm gay?

521
00:41:16,240 --> 00:41:17,640
I'll tell you then.

522
00:41:18,480 --> 00:41:21,800
David, that investor from Singapore,

523
00:41:22,360 --> 00:41:24,160
the one you're flaunting in my face,

524
00:41:25,880 --> 00:41:27,240
he's my boyfriend.

525
00:41:29,000 --> 00:41:33,520
I hired Parn to pretend to be my girlfriend
to make my parents happy.

526
00:41:34,800 --> 00:41:37,080
And I asked Parn to keep it a secret.

527
00:41:43,200 --> 00:41:45,160
You're saying I misunderstood?

528
00:42:03,920 --> 00:42:05,240
You misunderstood Parn.

529
00:42:06,840 --> 00:42:09,560
Don't wait until it's too late to get her back

530
00:42:09,560 --> 00:42:10,960
before you get yourself together.

531
00:42:11,760 --> 00:42:14,240
Even though we're business rivals,

532
00:42:14,960 --> 00:42:18,080
I'm rooting for you on this one.

533
00:42:20,720 --> 00:42:22,120
Because Parn really loves you.

534
00:43:20,800 --> 00:43:22,640
Pan Pastry-ne.

535
00:43:24,880 --> 00:43:26,000
Why "Ne"?

536
00:43:27,640 --> 00:43:29,160
What an unimpressive name.

537
00:43:32,920 --> 00:43:34,200
You're going out of business for sure.

538
00:43:45,960 --> 00:43:49,320
How well could someone like you
possibly run a shop?

539
00:44:03,640 --> 00:44:04,840
I knew it. It's just a small shop.

540
00:44:08,520 --> 00:44:09,640
Opening day.

541
00:44:16,160 --> 00:44:18,840
- First order!
- First order!

542
00:44:18,840 --> 00:44:22,680
Ms. Peem, what should we do with these?

543
00:44:22,680 --> 00:44:25,160
Bring me a box to try.
But I don't think it'll be good.

544
00:44:28,520 --> 00:44:29,520
Why didn't you accept the flowers?

545
00:44:29,520 --> 00:44:31,920
You have the right to send it.
I have the right not to accept.

546
00:44:33,320 --> 00:44:34,120
What's wrong with you?

547
00:44:34,120 --> 00:44:35,840
What is wrong with you?

548
00:44:35,840 --> 00:44:38,560
You say you don't want to see me,
but you keep coming.

549
00:44:40,480 --> 00:44:41,520
You don't love me anymore?

550
00:44:44,400 --> 00:44:51,320
♪ Even though my heart says I love you ♪

551
00:44:51,320 --> 00:44:56,320
♪ Why am I like this? ♪

552
00:44:56,840 --> 00:44:59,520
♪ I don't understand ♪

553
00:44:59,520 --> 00:45:04,920
♪ What's wrong with my mouth and my heart? ♪

554
00:45:04,920 --> 00:45:08,080
♪ Why won't they say the same thing? ♪
